 "notes": [
  "Manual text says 100 ohm resistors but the schematic label says 10k ohm; value=100 used per the hardware list.",
  "Fixed: each speaker's red (signal) leg and its resistor's top lead previously shared one hole. They now sit in different holes (rows g and f) of the same column strip (8b, 17b, 25b), so they are still electrically connected, as in the image.",
  "Breadboard hole names follow the image's row letters: the half with rows f-j (top of image) is written as bank 'b' and the half with rows a-e as bank 't', matching the catalogue's row-letter convention. Resistors bridge the centre gap.",
  "The speaker black legs go into the top rail nearest the black line (negative rail, 'tn'); exact rail hole numbers (tn.2, 9, 16, 24) are approximate since any hole in a rail strip is equivalent.",
  "Speaker port 1 is taken as the red (signal) leg, port 2 as the black (ground) leg.",
  "Arduino GND wire is plugged into the GND header next to pin 13 (GND.1 used); the speaker legs are inserted directly into the breadboard.",
  "Speakers on pins 8, 7 and 6 are in breadboard columns 8, 17 and 25 respectively."
